-- title:
--   Integer translation commutes with rectangular prism coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $R=\prod_{j=1}^d[\ell_j,u_j]$ be an integer rectangle with $\ell_j\le u_j$, let $a\in\mathbb Z^d$, and fix a coordinate $i$. Let $A_i=\{j\ne i:\ell_j<u_j\}$, $r\in I$, and $v\in[-1,1]^{A_i}$. The prism chart has coordinate $\ell_i+(u_i-\ell_i)r$ at $i$, midpoint plus $(u_j-\ell_j)v_j/2$ on active transverse coordinates, and $\ell_j$ on degenerate transverse coordinates. Identifying $A_i$ with the active coordinates of $R+a$, one has
--   $$\operatorname{prism}_{R+a,i}(r,v)=\operatorname{prism}_{R,i}(r,v)+a.$$
--   No positive width in coordinate $i$ is assumed.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (30 September 2026), Sections 2–7, supporting construction for Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39824v1. Formalization-specific helper: AbelianTargets/IntegerPrismTranslation.lean, lines 44–66; SHA256 631dff3119d4b0fcc5727eda728506a7c6c1f74be2d6ef82fb579483a5f06fac.

